r the exact same workloads.\n\nWhat it does: A tokenizer is a preprocessing tool that converts raw text into numerical IDs (tokens) that a neural network can process. Learn more\nhttps://www.anthropic.com/\n\n\nCheck out how different providers slice up: Hello World!\n\nGoogle: 3 tokens\n\nxAI: 3 tokens\n\nOpenAI: 3 tokens (9 billable)\n\nAnthropic: 5 tokens (11 billable)\n\nBottom line: Running Anthropic inputs and outputs costs more for the same data. LLM/LRM providers are in the business of selling tokens, so it's not shocking, but definitely worth factoring into pipeline budgets.\n\nFood for thought!\n2\nAdd reaction\n,\nMon 5:31 AM\n,\nTodd Christiansen\n,\nMon 10:33 AM\n,\nInteresting\n,\nMon 10:33 AM\n,\nWednesday, Aug 19\n11 unread,\nEric Smart\n,\nWed 8:23 AM\n,\n@\nRyan Kershaw\n I apologize for the high token usage this month. That is part of what I wanted to talk through tomorrow is potential ways to cut those costs on future runs of the reports I have been building for Bill.\n, 11 replies, Last Reply: Wed 8:37 AM\n,\nWed 8:23 AM\n,\nSheridan Richey, Eric Smart, and Ryan Kershaw replied\n11 unread\n11 replies\n, Last Reply\nWed 8:37 AM\nDevin Williams\n,\nWed 8:23 AM\n,\n@\nall\n A bit of a breakthrough on the AI Brunch and learns coming off GTS....good Capestone participation: Wayne, Vanessa, Noah Q, Juriaan, Jaco, Marlise and Thomas attended at least a portion of the meeting.\n, 13 replies, Last Reply: Wed 12:58 PM\n1\nAdd reaction\n,\nWed 8:23 AM\n,\n13 replies\n, Last Reply\nWed 12:58 PM\nRyan Kershaw\n,\nWed 1:48 PM\n,\nI've got the agenda made for tomorrow: \nAGC Weekly Meeting Agenda\n   \n@\nEric Smart\n I added your token conservation topic. I'd love to spend time tomorrow talking about wins or things you've built or MCPs you've been using. An open floor to hear new cool things you or your team has been doing with AI.\nAGC Weekly Meeting Agenda\nCopy link\nNo changes since last viewed by you\nSummarize this file\n,\nWed 1:48 PM\n,\nReply"}}"}

